@startuml Activity Diagram - UC-04 Manage Stocks

title Activity Diagram: UC-04 Manage Stocks

|Staff/Admin|
start
:Select "Manage Stocks" from Admin Panel Dashboard;

|System|
:Retrieve and display current stock levels, low-stock alerts, and item logs;

|Staff/Admin|
:Review current stock levels for products and raw ingredients;
:Input new stock shipments, adjust quantities manually, or update low-stock thresholds;
:Save the stocks updates;

|System|
:Validate inputs;
if (Inputs valid and non-negative?) then (Yes)
    :Record the updated stock quantities in the database;
    :Refresh the stocks view and display a confirmation message;
    if (Quantity below set threshold?) then (Yes)
        :Flag items as "Out of Stock" or trigger low-stock notifications;
    else (No)
    endif
else (No)
    :Highlight the invalid field, display an error message, and prevent saving until corrected;
endif

|System|
if (Order Event or Sync Occurs?) then (Order Placement)
    :Automatically check stock availability during checkout process;
    if (Sufficient stock?) then (Yes)
        :Proceed with order;
    else (No)
        :Flag the order item and notify customer with substitute or cancellation options;
    endif
else
    if (Order Event or Sync Occurs?) then (Order Confirmation)
        :Automatically deduct reserved quantities from stocks;
        if (Quantity drops below threshold?) then (Yes)
            :Trigger low-stock notifications or flag items as "Out of Stock";
        else (No)
        endif
    else
        if (Order Event or Sync Occurs?) then (Order Cancellation)
            :Automatically release reserved stock back into inventory;
        else (Third-Party Sync Failure)
            :Log the error and alert Staff/Admin to manually reconcile the stock count;
        endif
    endif
endif

|Staff/Admin|
stop

@enduml
